      "content": "My apologies for the confusion. Let's get straight to the technical details for calculating the Reorder Point (ROP) with safety stock to account for lead time variability.\n\nThe Reorder Point (ROP) formula is:\n\nROP = (Average Daily Usage x Lead Time) + Safety Stock\n\nTo calculate the Safety Stock, you can use the following formula:\n\nSafety Stock = Z x σLT x Average Daily Usage\n\nWhere:\n- Z is the Z-score corresponding to your desired service level (e.g., a Z-score of 1.65 corresponds to a 95% service level).\n- σLT is the standard deviation of lead time.\n- Average Daily Usage is the average number of units used per day.\n\nTo implement this in a spreadsheet, you would need to input your average daily usage, the lead time, the standard deviation of lead time, and the desired service level to calculate the safety stock. Then, you can use these values to calculate the ROP.\n\nFor example, if your average daily usage is 100 units, the lead time is 10 days, the standard deviation of lead time is 2 days, and you want a 95% service level (Z-score of 1.65), your safety stock would be:\n\nSafety",
