      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's much better, thanks. \n\nOne more thing—we've been seeing these weird, small discrepancies where the physical counts in the warehouse don't match our system records, almost like certain small components or cells are just quietly vanishing or getting miscounted during transit. It doesn't seem to follow a logical pattern of theft or shipping damage. How do I mathematically account for these kinds of irregular, \"unseen\" losses or \"phantom\" inventory issues in my calculations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
